    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d297-a5">

                <pb facs="0576" n="506" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg506"/>

                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Headquarters
                            Department of Dakota</hi>,<lb/><placeName><hi rendition="#italic">Fort
                                Snelling, Minn.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-05-20"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 20,
                        1883</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Official copy respectfully forwarded to headquarters Military Division of the
                    Missouri. I agree with Colonel Ruger that there is no reason to apprehend
                    anything more serious from the Crees than occasional “stealing raids,” which I
                    think can be controlled with the force available.</p>
                <closer><signed>ALFRED H. TERRY,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Brigadier-General,
                            Commanding.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
